-\caption{Effect of each action on traffic flow. Each panel is one junction seen
-top-down, the arterial running left to right with the cross street joining from
-above. In every panel the left of the stop line is the state at the decision
-instant (\textit{now}: hollow glyphs) and the right is the same stream
-after the action (\textit{after}: filled glyphs); the light pair at the top
-right is the \textit{current aspect}, main then cross, so the reader can see the
-light the action is taken on together with the flow it changes.
-(a) With no intervention the bus waits out the red and the queue behind it grows.
-(b) \texttt{GE} widens the arterial's green window by $\delta$, so the bus
-clears without stopping. (c) \texttt{GR} truncates the cross-street green by
-$\delta$, bringing the bus green forward. (d) \texttt{INS} adds a bus phase to
-the ring, so the bus is served this cycle instead of the next. (e) \texttt{ER}
-ends the bus phase once the bus has cleared, handing green to the cross street
-early. (f) \texttt{VP} drops an empty phase from the ring, removing two lost
-reds per cycle. (g) \texttt{PT} re-sequences the ring so the bus phase is served
-first. (h) Offset correction shifts the upstream green band by $\Delta$ so the
-bus arrives on green. Panels are schematic and carry no measured values.
-Panel (b) is enlarged in \cref{fig:ge_wave}.}
